From 211827fd7e7e0ea21172476891894843d1ac2308 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:01:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Neural Rendering menu: four task-ordered pages instead of
 seven

The seven NR pages split single decisions across pages (placement on one,
model resolution on another, its tiers on a third) and named the model's
weights "Preset 1/2/3, effect unverified". They are now:

- Main: weights (New / Original, with what the loaded nvngx_dlssnr.dll
  holds), look (with each look described in place), brightness (source in
  effect said in words, when to change it), where NR runs and speed.
- Fine-tune: everything else, by topic, in collapsible sections.
- Compare & Debug, and Optical F5Low, as before.

Text wraps at the pane edge everywhere, cards included (a child window
starts with wrapping off). Saved page names from the old layout open the
page their settings moved to.

Logic: one placement rule (ReadPlacement) instead of three copies; the
status says where the model actually ran (RanBeforeUpscale), so a
before-SR setting that cannot apply is reported instead of silently
ignored; quality tiers keep the placement; the 1/2/3 Pass buttons, which
also reset exposure behind the user's back, are gone; picking weights
sets every pass; the DLL version is read once, never searched for.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
